@startuml piece_detail_sequence
' ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
' piece_detail_sequence — v28.5, opening a piece from its parent's panel.
'
' The picture to hold: the DIALOG never navigates. It records where the
' user asked to go as part of its ANSWER (navigationTarget), and
' runTaskDetail — a loop, one live dialog at a time — acts on the record
' after applying. "Save-then-go": clicking through accepts; only Cancel
' discards. The one place the modal close/reopen hop lives is also the
' one function the future side-panel slice will swap.
'
' v28.6 NOTE: this modal loop is now runTaskDetail's FALLBACK — the
' docked TaskDetailPanel (detail_panel_states.*) is the preferred path,
' and its navigation is a swap-in-place with an unsaved-work guard.
'
' Referenced from design-addendum-subtasks.md §L.
' ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
!include _style.puml

actor User as U
participant "runTaskDetail\n(free function, the loop)" as R
participant "TaskDetailDialog\n(parent's panel)" as P
participant "TaskDetailDialog\n(piece's panel)" as C
participant "AppData\n(the single door)" as D

U -> R : click "Study for finals"
R -> D : taskById / subtasksOf (fresh read)
R -> P : construct + seedPieces\n(rows carry "Aug 8 · 45 min" hints)
U -> P : tick "Read the spec"
U -> P : click title "Chapter 3"
note right of P
  Records navigateTo = piece id,
  then accept() — the hop SAVES
  the sitting. Performs nothing.
end note
P --> R : Accepted
R -> D : applyTaskDetailAnswers\n(one Batch — the tick lands)
R -> R : taskId = navigationTarget()

R -> D : taskById (fresh again — never stale)
R -> C : construct + setBreadcrumb("‹ Study for finals")
note right of C
  A piece's panel: breadcrumb,
  no checklist (one level only).
  Full form — date, time, size.
end note
U -> C : set Aug 8 · 45 min, click breadcrumb
C --> R : Accepted (navigateTo = parent id)
R -> D : applyTaskDetailAnswers\n(the piece is now scheduled work)
R -> P : loop continues — parent reopens,\nrow now shows the chip

note over D
  Domain untouched by v28.5: a dated piece
  already flows into tasksDueOn and
  tasksNeedingBlock — the door was
  the only missing part.
end note

@enduml
